    "guide.deeds": "Rent is calculated when you collect it, not when you first looked. A mortgage blocks rent. A full color set doubles bare rent. Stations and utilities follow the active profile.",
    "guide.ip": "This is not an official Hasbro product. Street names and card wording are original. The classic numbers are a banker schedule you should still check against your physical edition — editions differ, and this profile is marked needs review.",
    "guide.limits": "Not in this version: official board names, automatic calendar interest, and sync across two phones. Loans do not tick by themselves; the banker accrues a period. A limited vault can refuse a building refund if the cash has already left the bank.",
    "guide.money": "Every cash move is a balanced posting: what leaves one account arrives in another. Undo puts the table back. Reverse is only for pure cash postings and writes an offsetting entry.",
    "guide.offline": "Games stay in this browser's IndexedDB after you close the tab. Export JSON if you want a file. After the app has loaded once, the installed copy is meant to reopen without a network. Do not rely on a CDN for fonts or rules.",
    "guide.play": "Create a game, seat two or more players, and start. The vault pays each starting stake. From the table you can pay, collect, transfer, and mark GO.",
    "guide.security": "There is no login. The browser sandbox is the only wall. Imported files are read as data and checked against the books. They are never executed.",
    "guide.trouble": "If someone cannot pay, sell buildings and mortgage first. Bankruptcy stays locked until those options are gone. The estate then goes to the bank or to one player.",
    "help.building": "Buildings and mortgage\n\nOwning a full color group lets you build houses evenly (never differing by more than one house), then a hotel on four full houses. Costs depend on the color group; selling back returns half. You may mortgage a deed for half its price — no rent while mortgaged — and unmortgage it later for 55% of the price.",
    "help.buying": "Buying and auctions\n\nLanding on an unowned deed lets you buy it for the listed price. If you decline, the bank auctions it: all players may bid and the highest bid wins. You cannot buy what you cannot afford.",
    "help.end": "Bankruptcy and winning\n\nIf you cannot pay a debt even after mortgaging and selling, you are bankrupt: your assets pass to the creditor (or the bank) and you leave the game. The last player standing wins — or, by agreement, after a fixed time the richest player (cash + deeds + buildings) wins.",
    "help.goal": "Goal\n\nMonopoly is a game of buying, renting and trading property. The aim is to bankrupt every other player: when a player cannot pay what they owe, they are out, and the last player standing wins.",
    "help.jail": "Jail\n\nYou go to jail by landing on Go to Jail, by a card, or by three doubles. Get out by paying 50, by rolling doubles within three turns, or with a Get Out of Jail card. Simply visiting the jail space costs nothing.",
    "help.rent": "Rent\n\nLanding on another player's deed means paying rent. Streets pay the base rent, doubled when the owner holds the whole color group with no buildings; houses and hotels pay by the rent table. Railroads pay 25 / 50 / 100 / 200 depending on how many the owner holds (a chance card may double it). Utilities pay the dice total × 4, or × 10 when both are owned. Mortgaged deeds collect no rent.",
    "help.setup": "Setup\n\nEach player starts with the starting cash (usually 1500). Pick a starting player and take turns clockwise. All deeds begin with the bank. The GO salary (usually 200) is paid when passing or landing on GO.",
    "help.title": "How to play",
    "help.turn": "A turn\n\nRoll two dice, move your token, then resolve the space: buy it, pay rent or tax, draw a card, or go to jail. Doubles grant another roll; three doubles in a row send you straight to jail.",
